# tests/golden/ and tests/adversarial/ pin exact bytes: golden.rs decodes a
# committed frame and asserts it equals the committed plaintext byte for
# byte, and torture.rs/adversarial.rs feed committed bytes straight to the
# decoder. Git's line-ending conversion must never touch either directory,
# on any platform, regardless of whether a given fixture's content looks
# like text (issue #518: Windows checkout rewrote a golden .plaintext
# fixture's LF line endings to CRLF, so the decoded frame no longer matched
# the pinned plaintext -- a checkout artifact, not a decode regression).
tests/golden/** -text
tests/adversarial/** -text
